# ===========================================================================
# Repo cleanliness policy (PR-4, 2026-05-06)
# ===========================================================================
#
# This .gitignore enforces a hard split between TRACKED source-of-truth
# files and MACHINE-LOCAL files generated by install/build/runtime:
#
#   TRACKED   — source code, templates that get COMPILED into machine-
#               local artifacts at install/build time (templates/, vendored
#               binaries with verified upstream provenance, etc.).
#   IGNORED   — anything that was generated for THIS machine (state/,
#               .venv/, .claude/agents/, .claude/skills/, .claude/logs/,
#               infrastructure/docker-compose.override.yml, vct-secrets/,
#               compiled __pycache__/, etc.).
#
# Why this matters: `update_orchestrator_at` (launcher) copies repo
# contents from one clone into another, so any gitignored file that
# IS still on disk in the source clone will silently propagate
# machine-to-machine if the copy walker is gitignore-blind. PR-4
# made the walker gitignore-aware; this file declares the policy.
#
# See `docs/REPO_CLEANLINESS.md` for the full canonical version.
# ===========================================================================

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Bug 31: launcher-managed compose override (per-machine volume location).
# Generated by `set_volumes_config_for_install` / `migrate_volumes`.
# PR-22 (2026-05-16): renamed to `compose.override.{yaml,yml}` so
# podman-compose's auto-loader recognizes it. Both extensions kept here
# so legacy hand-edited files stay ignored during the migration window.
infrastructure/compose.override.yaml
infrastructure/compose.override.yml
infrastructure/docker-compose.override.yml
infrastructure/docker-compose.override.yaml
# Per-machine vct-secrets PRIMITIVE. The user-side primitive lives at
# `~/.vct-secrets/`, never in the repo — this rule guards against an
# accidental `~/.vct-secrets/` symlink or copy ending up tracked.
# Anchored to repo root so it does NOT match `tools/vct-secrets/`,
# which is the CLI source code (legitimately tracked).
/vct-secrets/
*.pat
*.token
*.pem
*.key
!**/public.key
!**/*.pub.key
# `tools/vct-secrets/` is the CLI's source tree, NOT the secrets
# primitive's storage. Whitelist the tracked files explicitly so the
# `*.pat` / `*.token` / `*.pem` / `*.key` rules above don't false-
# positive on contributors who add new test fixtures or scripts under
# this dir.
!tools/vct-secrets/
!tools/vct-secrets/**

# Audit doc (only present on the OSS-readiness branch, not for main)
OSS_LAUNCH_READINESS.md

# Python build output (sdist/wheel). NOT the launcher's bundled prebuilt
# binaries at launcher/dist/ — those are checked in (see un-ignore below).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
/dist/
build/
.eggs/

# Launcher prebuilt binaries — checked in alongside source.
# See launcher/dist/README.md for the bundling rationale.
!launcher/dist/
!launcher/dist/**

# Diagnostic launcher builds (devtools-enabled, debug profile, etc.) —
# these are NOT shippable artifacts. Keep them out of the repo no matter
# where they land. The release binary lives ONLY at
# launcher/dist/<arch>/vct-launcher (un-ignored above).
launcher/dist/**/*-debug
launcher/dist/**/*-with-devtools
launcher/src-tauri/target/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
ENV/

# State (user-specific, never commit)
state/
*.pt
*.onnx

# Claude Code user-specific
.claude/logs/
.claude/logs/*.log
.claude/logs/*.jsonl
.claude/logs/.last_reviewed_commit
# kg-info / kg-search CLI telemetry (per-machine, created at script invocation)
claude_mcp_servers/weaviate_mcp/*_tool_usage.jsonl
.claude/cron-jobs.json
.claude/worktrees/
# Hook ephemeral state (per-session dedup, etc.)
.claude/state/
# Per-machine orchestrator install artifacts — populated by install.py, NEVER commit
.claude/agents/
.claude/skills/
# PR-39 (v0.2.12, 2026-05-16): the orchestrator-self's runtime .claude/{hooks,
# scripts,settings.json} are NOT shipped in the public repo. They are rendered
# from templates/ at install time by install.py::_materialize_orchestrator_self_claude_dir().
# Rationale: anything that is or will be generated from a template at install
# time should NOT ship in the public repo — only ship the template itself.
# The pre-PR-39 duplication was: 50 byte-identical hook files + 36 scripts +
# a bash-flavored Linux-only settings.json that broke on Windows installs.
.claude/hooks/
.claude/scripts/
.claude/settings.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Internal dev artifacts — must not be tracked in the public repo. The
# orchestrator-self's local .claude/context/ may exist on contributor
# machines (dated patch reports, code reviews, handoff notes between
# internal agent sessions) but is not for shipping. The release archive
# workflow at .github/workflows/release.yml already excludes
# .claude/context/ from release ZIPs; this rule blocks the same path at
# the git layer so dev artifacts can't slip into the public tree via
# `git add -A`. See PR-31 / Group L (v0.2.12) for the audit that
# surfaced 12 such files tracked at HEAD on 2026-05-16.
.claude/context/

# Per-machine secrets stash. Non-sensitive shared-with-Claude convention
# (the values inside ARE sensitive — bearer tokens, license keys — but
# the directory itself is a known location for Claude to read/write
# during a session). `*.token`/`*.pat` rules above already catch the
# obvious files; this is the directory-level belt-and-braces against an
# accidentally-committed README in the same dir.
.claude/secrets/

# pnpm artefacts — launcher uses npm; pnpm-lock.yaml accidentally created by
# contributors with pnpm on PATH must NOT enter the repo (would fight package-lock.json)
launcher/pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Paid-module manifests (Pro-tier, distributed via private repos +
# signed-URL gateway). The launcher's catalog discovery scans
# `<orchestrator_clone>/paid-modules/*/vct-module.json` IF the dir is
# present on disk (dev convenience), but the dir itself must NOT enter
# the public AGPL repo — each paid module's manifest ships from its
# OWN private repo (e.g. `hotak92/vct-rl-reranker` for the RL Reranker
# module). The container-pull installer recipe (manifest.rs::ContainerPull)
# is the production discovery path; this gitignore entry stops manifests
# from leaking via accidental `git add paid-modules/`. To work on a paid
# module locally, clone it into `paid-modules/<id>/` — the launcher will
# pick it up automatically without git tracking it.
paid-modules/

# IDE
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Test artifacts
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.log

# Container volumes (local)
weaviate_data/
ollama_data/

# Playwright per-session artifacts (config OK, outputs not)
.playwright-mcp/*.png
.playwright-mcp/*.log
.playwright-mcp/*.yml
.playwright-mcp/*.json
.playwright-mcp/*.html

# Debug screenshots dropped at repo root
*.png
!docs/**/*.png
!knowledge/**/*.png
# Launcher app icons (Tauri bundle inputs) and the SvelteKit static
# assets — both are legitimate tracked source. Without these
# exceptions, removing-and-re-adding any of these would require
# `git add -f`, and contributors hit a confusing "ignored" warning.
# (Audit 2026-05-06 §1: 18 PNGs were formally gitignored-but-tracked.)
!launcher/src-tauri/icons/**/*.png
!launcher/static/*.png

# MCP server caches
claude_mcp_servers/models_cache/
claude_mcp_servers/runs/

# VS Code per-user project settings (claude-code.env lives here, don't commit)
.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/settings.json.example

# Internal Lemon Squeezy inventory snapshots (contain customer/store IDs)
docs/license/LS_INVENTORY_*.md
docs/ADMIN_LICENSE.md

# ─── RL module (Pro-tier IP — NEVER in public AGPL repo) ────────────
# Actual model architecture, training loop, weights, and v2 log
# schema migration are maintained in a separate private upstream
# and shipped as signed binary via CDN, NOT as source. A development
# checkout may have them in the working tree (untracked) for
# convenience. Explicit gitignore so `git add -A` or a stray
# subagent commit can't accidentally publish them.
#
# `rl_kg_search.py` (a thin client that CALLS the RL server) and
# `rl_drain_citations.py` (the v0.2.70 turn-end deferred-citation drain,
# invoked by the Stop hook) are orchestrator-side CONSUMERS — they call the
# shared rl_client modules + the existing hub event route, not the model/
# training IP. Negate them explicitly so the broader pattern doesn't catch
# them.
claude_mcp_servers/rl_server/
claude_mcp_servers/scripts/rl_*.py
!claude_mcp_servers/scripts/rl_kg_search.py
!claude_mcp_servers/scripts/rl_drain_citations.py

# Developer-local one-off migration scripts. These run outside the
# launcher and may carry user-specific assumptions; not bundled.
scripts/migrate-shared-secrets.py
claude_mcp_servers/scripts/migrate_rl_log_*.py
claude_mcp_servers/scripts/offline_trainer*.py
claude_mcp_servers/scripts/retrieval_rl*.py
state/rl_*.pt
state/rl_*.json
state/rl_events*.jsonl
state/routing_*.jsonl
state/qlearning_*.json
tests/test_rl_*.py
tests/test_mcp_rl_*.py
# Also: the import-helper that pulls RL from the upstream
# orchestrator. Tracked elsewhere when needed.
vco_lib/import_from_orchestrator.py
tests/test_import_from_orchestrator.py
.logo-backup-*/
.claude/CONTEXT_STATE.md

# === VCO_dev operational leak guard (v0.2.50, 2026-06-08) ===
# Covers gaps identified in the v0.2.49 gitignore-and-remediation audit.
# These paths exist in the PRIVATE operational checkout but must NEVER ship in
# the public repo. The bundle-update flow copies un-gitignored files between
# clones, so an unguarded path = silent propagation.

# Root-level handoff narrative files (multi-agent / multi-chat coordination)
/HANDOFF-*.md

# Root-level MEMORY (project-local, not the global ~/.claude/projects/.../memory/)
/MEMORY.md

# .claude/ per-machine state not already covered above
.claude/MEMORY.md
.claude/PROJECT_REGISTRY.md
.claude/env
.claude/mockups/
.claude/rules/
.claude/.vco-manifest.json
.claude/metrics/
.claude/settings.json.bak-*

# VCT operational state outside .claude/
.vct/
/.vct-orchestrator-dev

# Knowledge graph private staging directories (drafts not for publication)
knowledge/inbox/
knowledge/daily/
knowledge/_drafts/

# VS Code per-machine tasks (settings.json already covered earlier)
.vscode/tasks.json

# Ad-hoc scratch scripts that accumulate at repo root
/assemble_pngs.py
/decode_canvas_png.py
/decode_chunks.py
/default_b64_chunk*.txt

# claude_mcp_servers compose overrides + backups
claude_mcp_servers/compose.override.yaml
claude_mcp_servers/compose.override.yml
claude_mcp_servers/*.bak-*
# ===========================================================================
# v0.2.51 cleanup additions (2026-06-09)
# Post-incident leak-hunt audit found these patterns leaking from VCO_dev
# operational state into public repo. Add to gitignore so they can't
# silently propagate again on next install/copy sweep.
# ===========================================================================

# Supabase CLI scratch state — contains live production project-ref +
# org_id + project name + pooler URL. Never commit; the maintainer's
# Supabase project ref is private operational data.
supabase/.temp/

# Internal maintainer-only docs — release procedures, demo-recording
# prep, launcher subtree workflow, unreleased licensing wire-up notes.
# The internal/ README itself says "Not user-facing. Excluded from
# release archives." — this gitignore enforces that intent.
/internal/

# VCO_dev private-fork pre-push guard installer scripts. These are
# helpers for OUR operational checkout, not user-facing tooling.
/tools/install-vco-dev-pre-push-guard.sh
/tools/install-vco-dev-pre-push-guard.ps1

# Completed one-off maintenance scripts. Historical operations that
# already ran; keep out of the public surface to avoid implying they're
# ongoing tools.
/scripts/add-silent-to-commands.py
/scripts/apply-branch-protection-v0.2.42.sh
/scripts/filter-repo-2026-05-06.sh

# Operations docs — maintainer-only deploy instructions (Supabase CI,
# release procedures, etc.). User-facing install/troubleshooting docs
# stay under docs/ directly.
/docs/operations/

# Release-narrative / version-specific docs that shouldn't survive
# beyond the release they describe.
/docs/v0.2.33-l0-deploy.md
/docs/codeql-triage-v*.md
/docs/EXCALIDRAW_WAYLAND_TEST.md
/docs/MAINTAINER_GUIDE.md
/docs/MIGRATION-0.2.0.md

# Internal CI dev notes (vs user-facing workflow docs which live
# elsewhere). The .github/workflows/README.md leaked our "Deferred for
# v0.2.30+" tracking narrative.
/.github/workflows/README.md

# Operational state generated post-install that must never be tracked.
# Already partially covered by HANDOFF-*.md / MEMORY.md / CONTEXT_STATE
# rules above; add the missing ones.
/UPDATE_DEFERRED.md
/SELF-HANDOFF-*.md
/HANDOFF-*-COMPREHENSIVE.md
/HANDOFF-FROM-*.md
/HANDOFF-TO-*.md
/HANDOFF-RL-*.md
.claude/context/audits/
.claude/context/plans/
.claude/context/pre-compact-snapshot.md
.claude/context/UPDATE_DEFERRED.md
.claude/context/SELF-HANDOFF-*.md
